menu "BOOTMUX router-spike safety"

config BOOTMUX_USB_NETWORK_EXPERIMENTAL
    bool "Enable experimental USB Ethernet/NCM interface"
    default n
    help
        Exposes the ESP32-S3 to the USB host as an Ethernet device and enables
        the USB-to-Wi-Fi routing experiment. Keep this disabled for normal
        BOOTMUX keyboard use. When disabled the USB configuration is HID-only,
        so plugging the S3 into a Mac cannot inject a DHCP lease, DNS server,
        or default route.

endmenu
